senses.gloss:
अर अर, अस्, आ, अम्, (fr. rt. ऋ), swift, speedy;
little; (at end of comp.) going; (अस्, अम्), m. n. the
spoke or radius of a wheel, see also अरम्, col. 3;
(अस्), m. a spoke of the time-wheel, viz. a Jaina divi-
sion of time, the sixth of an Avasarpiṇī or Utsarpiṇī;
the eighteenth Jaina saint of the present Avasarpiṇī;
N. of an ocean in Brahmā's world.
—अर-घट्ट or
अर-घट्टक, अस्, m. a wheel or machine for raising
water from a well (Hind. أرهٿ); a deep well.

अरक, अस्, m. the spoke of a wheel; a Jaina
division of time [cf. अर]; the plant Blyxa Octandra;
another plant, Gardenia Enneandra.

अरर अरर, अम्, n. a covering, a sheath;
(अस्, ई, अम्), m. f. n. the leaf of a door, a door; the
sheath of the shoot of a bamboo; (अस्), m. an awl;
a part of a sacrifice; fighting, war.

आ-राधित, अस्, आ, अम्, accomplished, effected;
propitiated, pleased; worshipped, honoured, rever-
enced.
